<h2 class="@DocsStyles.H2">Selector interfaces</h2>

<p class="@DocsStyles.P">
    The selector builder is a separate chain that produces a selector instead of a utility class. Like
    the builder, it is a sequence of stages enforced by the return types, so an invalid order such as a
    combinator after a pseudo-element does not compile.
</p>

<table class="@DocsStyles.Table">
    <thead class="@DocsStyles.Thead">
        <tr>
            <th class="@DocsStyles.Th">Interface</th>
            <th class="@DocsStyles.Th">Inherits</th>
            <th class="@DocsStyles.Th">What it is</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr class="@DocsStyles.Tr">
            <td class="@DocsStyles.Td"><code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">IBuildableSelector</code></td>
            <td class="@DocsStyles.Td"><code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">&mdash;</code></td>
            <td class="@DocsStyles.Td">A finished selector or selector list. <code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">Css</code> returns the full text including any theme prefix and at-rule wrapper.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="@DocsStyles.Tr">
            <td class="@DocsStyles.Td"><code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">IPseudoElementBuilder</code></td>
            <td class="@DocsStyles.Td"><code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">IBuildableSelector</code></td>
            <td class="@DocsStyles.Td">The terminal stage for pseudo-elements. <code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">PseudoElement</code> closes the selector; <code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">FunctionalPseudoElement</code> returns to the compound stage.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="@DocsStyles.Tr">
            <td class="@DocsStyles.Td"><code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">ICompoundSelectorBuilder</code></td>
            <td class="@DocsStyles.Td"><code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">IPseudoElementBuilder</code></td>
            <td class="@DocsStyles.Td">The compound stage: classes, ids, attributes, pseudo-classes and combinators. Every method returns the same stage, so modifiers chain in any order.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="@DocsStyles.Tr">
            <td class="@DocsStyles.Td"><code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">ITargetSelectorBuilder</code></td>
            <td class="@DocsStyles.Td"><code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">ICompoundSelectorBuilder</code></td>
            <td class="@DocsStyles.Td">Adds <code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">Element</code>, the type selector such as <code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">div</code>.</td>
