<h2 class="@DocsStyles.H2">BaseStyleBuilder&lt;T&gt;</h2>

<p class="@DocsStyles.P">
    <code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">BaseStyleBuilder&lt;T&gt;</code> is the abstract class that
    implements <code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">IStyleBuilder&lt;T&gt;</code> once for every builder.
    It owns the class-name list, the theme/media/pseudo context and the
    <code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">Important</code> scoping model. Its constructor is
    <code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">private protected</code>, so even though the type is public it is
    not a supported extension point outside the assembly: derive from it only if you are adding a
    builder inside FluentCss itself. For application-level helpers, write extension methods on
    <code class="@DocsStyles.InlineCode">IStyleBuilder&lt;T&gt;</code> instead, as shown on
    <a href="/docs/extensibility" class="@DocsStyles.Link">Extensibility</a>.
</p>

<CodeBlock Code="@BaseStyleBuilderApi" />

